 different direction so  i think that my my role in as defense  procurement uh was fascinating and i was  able to bring two key uh  new pieces of uh kit into into being if  that's the way you describe them and you  know real honor to know that as i now  watch it all being built and it's the  next generation of both our army and our  navy's kit that's extraordinary to think  that i was able to help  uh you know get that into place um but  it was as much as i think it was a real  apprenticeship on how the machinery of  government fits together and you  mentioned civil servants how they would  work for ministers i just wanted on that  i mean  there are some in the government who  have quite an interesting rhetoric on  civil servants and whether it's you know  working from home or i think jacob reese  morgan has recently been doing sport  check and inspections  is your view that civil servants do do  a lot of good i actually  generally speaking want to work with the  government so yes jacob i hear was  crawling through our corridors in uh  department of international trade the  other day but as i've got the top  statistics of any department mostly  because i've got a fantastic team of  young people and they were very keen to  come back to work i think we passed the  jacob rees-mob test so that was good um  civil servants are amazing people it's  an incredibly um  sort of deep relationship they have  government they have they move around  through their careers and they bring  with them this extraordinary uh  understanding of how the complexity of a  machinery of government works uh clearly  there are some who are uh you know uh  more highly skilled in certain areas i  think when uh some people say you know  they don't do what they should my  experience has been uh they're  very very uh literate very good on  policy i i've i'm always seeking out  people who are good at data analytics  who will  use data because i'm a mathematician  that's how i think so where's the data  