ics uh  you know midterm by-elections you know  invariably do give the government a  hammering you know hartlepool was a  notable exception uh which was ensued  fantastic it was wonderful to welcome  jill mortimer into the house with us but  it is relatively normal for uh  by-elections midterm to see the  government of the day uh get a trouncing  and i hope very much that when the next  general election comes tiverton and  hunter will be returned blue without  question  it's probably worthwhile it is the  biggest by-election defeat in history if  you look at the numbers i think  um now just finally the final question  is when we ask everyone on this podcast  which is just what is the worst advice  you've ever been given which you kind of  ignored or you could have taken it on  board and then thought why did i follow  that  that's a really interesting question uh  i listen to everything people say  and i reach my own judgment i think my  mother would say i'm probably not very  good at taking advice  uh i disagree i think i hear what  everyone says but i will filter it in my  own way so i don't think  i would say anyone's given me good or  bad advice people can tell me what they  like and i will note it  and ponder it and filter it through the  amt view of the world and then reach a  decision so i wouldn't chastise anyone  for giving me bad advice i probably just  dismissed it on the way through she's  still wearing your boss t-shirt  metaphorically so it's still there  under my shirt like a superman t-shirt  um thank you for joining us today it's a  pleasure  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

